  <text>
      <body>
         <entry xml:id="gastra-dlgenr"
            xml:lang="en"
            type="mainEntry"
            prev="#"
            next="#"
            source="Genesis Rabbah">
            <form type="lemma" opt="false">
               <orth type="lemma" xml:lang="jpa" opt="false" select="true">גסטרא</orth>
               <orth type="transliteration" xml:lang="fjb" opt="false">gsṭrʾ</orth>
               <pron notation="rabbinic" opt="false">gasṭraʾ</pron>
            </form>
            <form type="inflected">
               <orth type="inflected" xml:lang="jpa">גסטריות</orth>
               <orth type="transliteration" xml:lang="fjb">gsṭrywt</orth>
               <pron notation="rabbinic">gasṭriyot</pron>
               <gramGrp>
                  <gram type="num">pl.</gram>
               </gramGrp>
            </form>
            <sense xml:id="gastra-dlgenr-1">
               <cit type="translation" xml:lang="en" subtype="sense">
                  <quote>military camp, fort</quote>
               </cit>
               <cit type="translationEquivalent" xml:lang="la">
                  <quote>castra</quote>
               </cit>
               <cit type="example" xml:lang="jpa">
                  <quote>ויאמר י"י אמחה וגו' [מהן סבורין 
                     <app>
                        <lem>גסטריות</lem>
                        <rdg wit="#Vat1">אהליות וקסוסטריות</rdg>
                        <rdg wit="#Vat2">עלייות וגסטריות</rdg>
                        <rdg wit="#K">חיילו' גסטריו</rdg>
                        <rdg wit="#V">אריות גסטריות</rdg>
                        <rdg wit="#Ox1">עליות וגיסטריות</rdg>
                     </app> אני צריך] הלא בדבר בראתי את העולם אני מוצא ומכלה אותן</quote>
                  <bibl>
                     <ref type="witness">28,2</ref>
                     <ref type="witness">I 260: 12</ref>
                  </bibl>
                  <cit type="translation" xml:lang="en">
                     <quote>And the Lord said: I will blot out man. ‘What do they think? That I need military camps [to combat them]? Did I not create the world with a word? I will utter a word and destroy them. (cf. Freedman / Simon I 224)</quote>
                  </cit>
                  <note>= <bibl type="ancient">Yalq 47 [13b: 37]</bibl> (<term xml:lang="jpa">חיילות גיסטריות</term>)</note>
               </cit>
            </sense>
            <note>For sg. see e.g. <bibl type="ancient">bShab 121a</bibl>. Cf. <bibl type="modern">Levy I 350a</bibl>. Acc. to Levy in the version of V <term xml:lang="jpa">ריות גסטריות</term> the word may be understood as adj. Gr. <term xml:lang="grc">γάστρις</term>, i. e. “obese lions”. Cf. <bibl type="modern">Jastrow I 260b</bibl>. To distinguish from <term xml:lang="jpa">גסטרא</term> <term xml:lang="fjb">gsṭrʾ</term> <term xml:lang="rabbinic">gasṭraʾ</term> Gr. <term xml:lang="grc">γάστρα</term> (<bibl type="modern">Krauss, LW II 180b-181a</bibl>; <bibl type="modern">Heijmanns [2013] 80-81</bibl>). For the spelling <term xml:lang="jpa">קסטרה</term> <term xml:lang="en">gsṭrh</term> <term xml:lang="rabbinic">qastrah</term>, <term xml:lang="jpa">קסטרא</term> <term xml:lang="fjb">qsṭrʾ</term> <term xml:lang="rabbinic">qasṭrʾ</term>, cf. <bibl type="modern">Sokoloff, DJPA 570a</bibl>, <bibl type="modern">Krauss, LW II 557ab</bibl>. The reading in Vat 1 is probably influenced by <term xml:lang="jpa">גזוזטראות</term> <term xml:lang="fjb">gzwzṭrʾwt</term>, sg. <term xml:lang="jpa">גזוזטרא</term> <term xml:lang="fjb">gzwzwṭrʾ</term> <term xml:lang="rabbinic">gezuzṭraʾ</term> Gr. <term xml:lang="grc">ἐξώστρα</term> (<bibl type="modern">Heijmanns [2013] 75-76)</bibl>.</note>
            <ref type="bibliography">
               <bibl>
                  <title>Krauss, LW II</title>
                  <citedRange>181b</citedRange>
               </bibl>
            </ref>
         </entry>
      </body>
